current_state:
  - MiniModel.org is the Rust-first P2P tiny model package exchange roadmap site.
  - Source options are user-owned local files/lists, user-triggered Hugging Face discovery, local Hugging Face conversion-request/script handoff, local share metadata export after verified `.slm` import, direct known-peer HTTP piece serve/fetch, and future broader P2P discovery/relay; all converge on local `.slm` verification.
  - First implementation code now includes a standard-library Rust verifier workspace: `crates/minimodel-core` plus `crates/minimodel`, real q8 fixture manifest, local `.slm` artifact verification, chunk/Merkle checks, local peer-piece export, direct HTTP peer-piece serving/fetch with project-server host rejection, peer-piece reassembly, and basename-only import receipts.
  - The live public-safe export is verified.
  - Direct public .uai and agent-file-handoff access is denied.
